Source: motanka-core
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruslan Babych <1285978+digitwolf@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               python3,
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/digitwolf/motanka
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/digitwolf/motanka
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/digitwolf/motanka.git

Package: motanka-core
Architecture: all
Depends: dbus-user-session,
         dconf-cli,
#if noble
         motanka-stack (>= 0.1.0-1~ubuntu24.04.1),
         motanka-stack-shell (>= 0.1.0-1~ubuntu24.04.1),
#endif
#if resolute
         motanka-stack (>= 0.1.0-1~ubuntu26.04.1),
         motanka-stack-shell (>= 0.1.0-1~ubuntu26.04.1),
#endif
         pkexec,
         python3,
         python3-dbus,
         python3-xdg,
         systemd,
         util-linux-extra,
         @PKGMAP_DEPENDS@
         ${misc:Depends},
Description: Omarchy-compatible Hyprland session for Ubuntu - core
 Motanka is an Omarchy-compatible Hyprland layer for Ubuntu. It installs
 next to the current desktop as a separate login session, follows
 upstream Omarchy, and removes cleanly.
 .
 This package holds the motanka command, upstream Omarchy at the pinned
 commit (unmodified, in /opt/motanka/share/omarchy), the compatibility
 layer that runs it on Ubuntu (command wrappers, shims, overrides, the
 package map and the polkit-authorised helper), and the Motanka login
 session with its user units, dconf profile and portal configuration.
